\f4\fs26 Since the wedding, Cracker had been hiding out in his safe-house and had kept a low profile. Hayley and Kathy seemed to have dumped him, neither having the time to return his calls. He had been receiving regular reports of the tunneling efforts, but had not managed to get off the couch and show himself on site. He could not do much to help as progress had slowed, the excavating Elvi having now resorted to jack-hammers and hand tools, but the goal was in site. He had not received any notifications from Agent Jones and feared Proactive Reciprocity would win the race. He decided he had better chase it up.\
He left the building and headed for the travelator. The Elvi had re-taken vast sections of the circle of carriages and it had become a popular, mostly safe mode of transport. As he wandered aimlessly towards the Management Zone border wall, he was struck in the head from behind and fell to the clean paving bricks. He attempted to stand up and protest, but he was struck several more times before finally losing consciousness.\
\'93Wake up, wake up.\'94 Haloren yelled in his face. \'93How fucking hard is your head? I am surprised you are still breathing!\'94\
\'93How did you find me?\'94 Cracker said rubbing his head ruefully.\
\'93You didn\'92t think I would recognise you at the reception? That was the...\'94\
\'93The worst disguise ever. I have been told. To be fair, it was only meant to fool Shakti. How was I supposed to know you were going to be there?\'94\
\'93That is of no importance now. What it of importance is you. I saw you shot 3 times, point blank. How did you survive?\'94 Halo thought there must have been some Hollywood trickery, but the footage was very convincing. He ripped open Cracker\'92s shirt and saw no ghastly blast wounds, virtually nothing. A few pink dots. Halo\'92s face bore testimony to a few adolescent zits that had left far worse scars. \'93Ha, I knew it. It was smoke and mirrors.\'94\
\'93Yeah, you got me. Are you going to give me up to the cops? If they find out I am still alive, they will arrest or kill me.\'94 Cracker didn\'92t like the direction of this conversation and knew he would have a better chance with the cops, but was still hopeful of a reprieve. He looked around for an exit but there were no windows and only one door. \'93Only one door? Where is this place? Everything looks old and decayed. The Pale?\'94\
\'93We are in a safe location. That is all you need to know. Now what I need to know is simple. How did you get the credit for my work?\'94 \
\'93Your work? What are you talking about?\'94\
\'93They think you are the Nightclub Vampire.\'94\
\'93Oh, shit.\'94 Was all Cracker could think to say. Halo confirmed he was the most prolific serial killer in the history of the Primary Trade Dominion. 
\f5\i Shit! 
\f4\i0 Cracker did not believe it, even though he had just heard an unsolicited confession.\
\'93I cannot let that stand. You don\'92t have the brain power to pull it off. Why would they think it was you?\'94\
\'93The Commissioner set it all up. I was supposed to be charged and eliminated in my cell. I have no idea why. I have never met him and I was lucky I happened to be with Shakti the night of one of the killings\'94 He prudently omitted Sarah\'92s name. He did not want her name ringing in the ears of a serial killer.\
\'93James Marrin? That one was a real bonus.\'94 Halo reflected back to the night of the bombing. He had been looking for James Marrin and he had just presented himself. Such a fortunate happenstance. \'93He had to be ticked off the list. He had tried to get close to you through Andrea Novetine. They both had to go.\'94\
\'93That\'92s a pretty weird looking knife you got there. What is it?\'94 Cracker asked, not really wanting to know the answer.\
\'93My best friend.\'94 Halo replied.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0

